WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.811 --> 00:00:16.653
was still talking to Barry and Mateo about the cook-off.

2
00:00:16.673 --> 00:00:22.377
"If we win the contest, I'm going to use my prize money for cooking classes," Barry said.

3
00:00:22.397 --> 00:00:27.781
"And I'm going to buy a collector's edition of the first Cosmic Quest comic book.

4
00:00:28.781 --> 00:00:29.962
They're expensive!"

5
00:00:30.262 --> 00:00:30.943
Mateo said.

6
00:00:30.963 --> 00:00:32.788
"What about you, Ally?"

7
00:00:32.808 --> 00:00:33.369
Barry asked.

8
00:00:34.269 --> 00:00:35.410
Ally scratched her head.

9
00:00:35.430 --> 00:00:37.672
"I can't think of anything I need."

10
00:00:37.692 --> 00:00:40.954
"I bet you'll come up with something," Barry said.

11
00:00:40.974 --> 00:00:45.757
"So, tell us more about Food Truck Rally, Barry," Ally said.

12
00:00:45.777 --> 00:00:50.180
"Yeah, what other local food trucks are going to be in the contest?"

13
00:00:50.501 --> 00:00:51.241
Mateo asked.

14
00:00:51.261 --> 00:00:53.283
"They sent me a list."

15
00:00:53.783 --> 00:00:55.004
Barry pulled out his phone.

16
00:00:55.684 --> 00:01:00.508
"There's Taco Nation, Gimme the Beef, Ella's Eats, the Food Dude, and us."

17
00:01:01.772 --> 00:01:04.534
"That's only five food trucks," Ally said.

18
00:01:04.554 --> 00:01:07.776
"You said that the contest was among six trucks."

19
00:01:08.916 --> 00:01:09.537
"You're right."

20
00:01:10.117 --> 00:01:11.558
Barry scanned the list again.

21
00:01:11.578 --> 00:01:13.999
"Oh," he said, biting his lip.

22
00:01:14.019 --> 00:01:16.661
"I didn't see the last truck on the list."

23
00:01:17.321 --> 00:01:18.902
"So, who is it?"

24
00:01:19.363 --> 00:01:20.123
Mateo asked.

25
00:01:20.843 --> 00:01:22.024
Barry held up his phone.

26
00:01:22.044 --> 00:01:26.447
"What?" Mateo's eyes went wide as he stared at the screen.

27
00:01:26.467 --> 00:01:31.658
"Pepe's? Since when do they have a food truck?"

28
00:01:32.538 --> 00:01:33.179
Barry shrugged.

29
00:01:33.199 --> 00:01:35.701
"Their website says it's brand-new."

30
00:01:36.542 --> 00:01:37.643
Ally's eyes flashed.

31
00:01:38.223 --> 00:01:40.765
"Pepe's almost cost Ray his business once!

32
00:01:41.205 --> 00:01:42.667
We cannot let them win.

33
00:01:43.447 --> 00:01:50.193
Barry, you should come up with something really fantastic to serve at the contest, something guaranteed to win!"

34
00:01:50.213 --> 00:01:52.955
"Yeah," Mateo said.

35
00:01:52.975 --> 00:01:55.377
"Something that no one will be expecting."

36
00:01:55.397 --> 00:01:57.118
"I'm already on it!"

37
00:01:57.619 --> 00:01:59.080
Barry hurried out of the diner.

38
00:02:01.908 --> 00:02:05.230
"So, let's talk about our double date," Mateo said to Ally.

39
00:02:05.250 --> 00:02:08.272
"What do kids on Astralia do on dates?"

40
00:02:09.673 --> 00:02:12.936
"Stardust catching is really popular," Ally said.

41
00:02:12.956 --> 00:02:16.398
"We wear special spacesuits and collect stardust."

42
00:02:18.639 --> 00:02:21.021
"That sounds like fun," Mateo said.

43
00:02:21.041 --> 00:02:26.465
"But we've got too much gravity here on Earth to go stardust catching."

44
00:02:26.485 --> 00:02:31.008
"Are you going to take my advice and plan a double date?"

45
00:02:31.468 --> 00:02:33.469
Flo asked as she came out of the kitchen.

46
00:02:34.009 --> 00:02:34.630
Ally nodded.

47
00:02:34.650 --> 00:02:36.651
"We're trying to think of what to do."

48
00:02:36.671 --> 00:02:41.333
"What about going to the park on Saturday night to watch the lunar eclipse?

49
00:02:42.134 --> 00:02:44.015
You can have a picnic," Flo said.

50
00:02:44.935 --> 00:02:47.557
She looked up as two customers walked into the diner.

51
00:02:47.577 --> 00:02:49.558
"You stay here, Ally.

52
00:02:50.058 --> 00:02:50.899
I'll get their order."

53
00:02:50.919 --> 00:02:53.280
"Thanks, Flo," Ally said.

54
00:02:53.300 --> 00:02:56.041
"I'm always here for you, Ally."

55
00:02:57.202 --> 00:02:58.042
Flo hurried off.

56
00:02:58.062 --> 00:03:01.789
"I like Flo's idea," Mateo said.

57
00:03:01.809 --> 00:03:04.571
"Ally, you should just call Julius.

58
00:03:05.112 --> 00:03:08.054
Girls ask boys out on dates all the time here."

59
00:03:09.075 --> 00:03:14.039
"We do too on Astralia, but I don't have time to spend a full day serenading him in

60
00:03:14.080 --> 00:03:17.603
public." "Huh?"

61
00:03:18.163 --> 00:03:19.564
Mateo looked confused.

62
00:03:19.584 --> 00:03:23.288
"That's what we do on Astralia," Ally said.

63
00:03:23.308 --> 00:03:28.052
"We follow the person around and sing their favorite songs to them all day long."

64
00:03:30.724 --> 00:03:33.665
"That sounds like a lot," Mateo said.

65
00:03:33.685 --> 00:03:36.346
"Calling him might be easier."

66
00:03:38.027 --> 00:03:39.968
Ally gulped, suddenly worried.

67
00:03:39.988 --> 00:03:42.709
"What if he's changed his mind about me?

68
00:03:43.449 --> 00:03:45.670
Or maybe he figured out that I'm an alien!

69
00:03:46.631 --> 00:03:47.931
Do you think he'd tell Dr.

70
00:03:47.991 --> 00:03:53.213
Lloyd?" "You're being silly," Mateo said.

71
00:03:53.233 --> 00:03:56.295
"Okay, I'll do it."

72
00:03:57.015 --> 00:03:59.696
Ally pulled Alpha out of her pocket and powered her up.

73
00:04:01.568 --> 00:04:03.329
"Alpha, call Julius."

74
00:04:04.189 --> 00:04:05.510
Alpha made a snorting sound.

75
00:04:05.530 --> 00:04:10.912
"Fine." Ally held her breath, waiting for Julius to answer.

76
00:04:11.513 --> 00:04:14.054
But after one ring, the line went dead.

77
00:04:14.074 --> 00:04:16.895
"That's strange," Ally said.

78
00:04:16.915 --> 00:04:19.696
"Alpha, call Julius."

79
00:04:20.197 --> 00:04:22.898
Again, the phone rang once and went dead.

80
00:04:24.879 --> 00:04:27.480
Ally tried two more times and then gave up.

81
00:04:29.580 --> 00:04:31.522
"He doesn't want to talk to me."

82
00:04:31.542 --> 00:04:33.664
Mateo shook his head.

83
00:04:33.684 --> 00:04:36.687
"It's probably just Alpha glitching again.

84
00:04:38.628 --> 00:04:40.230
Try calling him with my phone."

85
00:04:41.431 --> 00:04:42.312
Ally hesitated.

86
00:04:42.332 --> 00:04:45.374
"Do you want me to call him?"

87
00:04:45.735 --> 00:04:46.455
Mateo asked.

88
00:04:46.475 --> 00:04:49.418
"No, that's silly," Ally said.

89
00:04:49.438 --> 00:04:53.262
"I'll do it, but after work and at home, in private.

90
00:04:53.982 --> 00:04:55.564
Maybe I'll be less nervous then."

91
00:05:00.016 --> 00:05:02.277
But later, Ally felt just as anxious.

92
00:05:03.657 --> 00:05:06.398
She paced around her room with Mateo's phone in her hand.

93
00:05:06.418 --> 00:05:09.739
"I don't know why I'm so nervous, Alpha.

94
00:05:10.319 --> 00:05:11.499
It's just a phone call.

95
00:05:12.180 --> 00:05:15.301
But what if he picks up this time and I don't know what to say?"

96
00:05:15.321 --> 00:05:19.482
"Preparation is the key to any task," Alpha said.

97
00:05:19.502 --> 00:05:21.742
"You're right, Alpha!

98
00:05:22.403 --> 00:05:24.643
I'm glad to see you working perfectly now.

99
00:05:25.123 --> 00:05:26.564
That gives me a good idea.

100
00:05:27.356 --> 00:05:31.298
Write me a script of what to say to Julius."

101
00:05:31.958 --> 00:05:32.679
Alpha growled.

102
00:05:33.099 --> 00:05:34.499
"I am not a toy!"

103
00:05:34.519 --> 00:05:37.441
"I know," Ally said.

104
00:05:37.461 --> 00:05:40.882
"But your prime directive is to assist me."

105
00:05:40.902 --> 00:05:43.584
"Fine." Alpha grumbled.

106
00:05:44.084 --> 00:05:45.805
A short script appeared on the screen.

107
00:05:45.825 --> 00:05:47.345
"Thank you!"

108
00:05:47.806 --> 00:05:48.326
Ally said.

109
00:05:48.346 --> 00:05:52.708
"I'm finally ready to make this call!"
